Patch to smithay-clipboard, the Wayland clipboard and drag-and-drop code
under libcosmic's iced (#81): a drop is read from the seat that has the drag
offer when smithay-clipboard doesn't know a "latest seat" yet (it learns it
from a click or key press on one of the client's surfaces). Without it, the
first drag onto the shell's desktop after signing in, made before touching the
shell, didn't land.

Applied by packaging/arch/PKGBUILD (_patch_smithay_clipboard) to the copy in
Lapin's private cargo home (cargo-lapin), which builds the shell.

In a sandbox: `git apply` it in
~/.cargo/git/checkouts/smithay-clipboard-*/859b02c, then
`cargo clean -p smithay-clipboard` before building the shell: cargo doesn't
notice edited git checkouts.
